        <mxCell id="IClw5t5dYYrdMW6lydoo-7" value="1. User Clicks &quot;Create Group&quot;&lt;br&gt;2. Frontend requests credentials from Keycloak&lt;br&gt;3. Keycloak either tells the frontend to login again, or gives the credentials&lt;br&gt;4. Backend recieves request to create new group given user token, new group name, and event.&lt;div&gt;5. Backend notifies Keycloak to create a new group with the &quot;Owner&quot;, &quot;Admin&quot;, and &quot;Member&quot; subgroups. It then adds the user to the &quot;Owner&quot; subgroup. If event was specified and is valid, it will also add the group to the given event.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;6. Backend Creates an join code for the group, and stores all relevant group information in the database.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;7. Backend returns the group information to the Frontend&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="640" y="40" width="200" height="400" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
